      "text": "Plugging in the coordinates $(6, 10)$ into both equations gives us two simultaneous equations involving $m$ and $b$.\n\nFor the first line, $y = mx + 4$, substituting the point $(6, 10)$ yields:\n\\[10 = 6m + 4\\]\n\nFor the second line, $y = 3x + b$, substituting the point $(6, 10)$ yields:\n\\[10 = 3(6) + b\\]\n\nLet's solve these equations to find $m$ and $b$.\n\nFor the first equation:\n\\[10 = 6m + 4\\]\n\\[6 = 6m\\]\n\\[m = 1\\]\n\nFor the second equation:\n\\[10 = 18 + b\\]\n\\[b = 10 - 18\\]\n\\[b = -8\\]\n\nThus, $b + m = -8 + 1 = -7$.\n\nThe value of $b + m$ is $\\boxed{-7}$.",
